 Research title: "Comparative Analysis of Successful and Failed Enterprise System Implementations"

Case Study 1: Successful Enterprise System Implementation by N&N Moving Supplies

    Company Overview
        N&N Moving Supplies, a family-run distributor of moving equipment, expanded from one to three locations, significantly increasing its workforce. The company initially relied on QuickBooks and a third-party payroll provider but struggled with tracking time records and reconciling payroll with financial accounts. To streamline operations and improve efficiency, N&N implemented NetSuite ERP.

    Implementation Process
        To ensure a smooth transition, N&N partnered with NOVAtime to integrate a time-clock solution within NetSuite ERP. This integration aimed to automate payroll, enhance financial tracking, and provide employees with access to personalized dashboards via iPads at each site. The company prioritized user training and change management to maximize adoption.

    Key Success Factors

        • Employee Buy-in: Personalized dashboards and proactive communication ensured user adoption.
        • Strategic Partnerships: Collaboration with NOVAtime helped tailor the ERP system to N&N’s needs.
        • Process Automation: Automated payroll and financial tracking reduced errors and administrative workload.
        • Cross-location Visibility: Real-time labor cost tracking improved financial decision-making.

    Outcomes & Impact

        • 84% Reduction in Payroll Processing Time: Automation streamlined calculations and approvals.
        • Faster Account Balancing & Improved Accuracy: Enhanced reconciliation of financial records.
        • Enhanced Workforce Management: Employees gained real-time access to work hours, leave balances, and performance metrics.
        • Data-driven Decision-Making: Insights into labor cost trends supported better financial planning and resource allocation.